==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ten-}}
From {{uder|en|xno|maintenour}}, {{uder|en|fro|mainteneor}}, from {{m|fro|maintenir||to maintain}}; with later remodelling of the suffix after {{m|en|-er}}. {{surf|en|maintain|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/meɪnˈteɪnə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-maintainer.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪnə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[keeps]] or [[upholds]] something; a {{l|en|steward}}.
#: {{ux|en|He become the '''maintainer''' of the software project.}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Matthew|V|text=Blessed are the '''maynteyners''' of peace: for they shalbe called the chyldren of God.}}
# A person who does [[maintenance]] work.
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Steve Almasy and Chris Boyette|title=Lost hiker’s message: Please call husband when my body is found|url=https://www.cnn.com/2016/05/26/us/missing-hiker-gerry-largay-last-messages/index.html|date=2016-05-26|passage=“In somm trouble. Got off trail to go to br. Now lost. Can u call AMC to c if a trail '''maintainer''' can help me. Somewhere north of woods road. Xox,” she wrote.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004030643/https://www.cnn.com/2016/05/26/us/missing-hiker-gerry-largay-last-messages/index.html|archivedate=4 October 2022}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Oren Liebermann|title=CENTCOM disputes Air Force account of attempted hijacking at Kabul airport during Afghanistan evacuation|url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/14/politics/afghanistan-withdrawal-kabul-airport-attempted-hijacking/index.html|date=2021-10-14|passage=“To stay open, the senior enlisted leader of U.S. Forces-Afghanistan Forward said he needed people to cover security,” Duncan wrote. “Personnel Recovery Task Force (PRTF) Pilots, '''maintainers''' and support personnel donned their vests, helmets and M-4 rifles and manned defensive fighting positions.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260403013302/https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/14/politics/afghanistan-withdrawal-kabul-airport-attempted-hijacking/index.html|archivedate=3 April 2026}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Helen Regan, Taylor Romine, Dalia Faheid, et. al.|title=January 30, 2025 - DC plane collision news|url=https://www.cnn.com/us/live-news/plane-crash-dca-potomac-washington-dc-01-29-25/index.html|date=2025-01-30|passage=Muehlendorf told CNN that O’Hara was a crew chief by trade, explaining that his “military occupational specialty was a 15T and he was originally trained to be a '''maintainer''' of Black Hawk helicopters.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260522020920/https://www.cnn.com/us/live-news/plane-crash-dca-potomac-washington-dc-01-29-25/index.html|archivedate=22 May 2026}}
# {{lb|en|dentistry}} A [[device]] used to keep [[teeth]] in a given [[position]].

